{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.no_traceFunctional_of_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.no_traceFunctional_of_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L190-L200","doc":"**The falsifiable form**, and the one AME2020 instantiates: a binding with any\nnonzero connected three-body cumulant is not `f ∘ trace` for **any** `f` carrying\nproducts to sums, over **any** bond-rule trace. This excludes the whole family at\nonce rather than one `f` at a time — which is what makes it an answer to\n`qou-edt7` rather than another candidate for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.b4_eq_zero_of_bondRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.b4_eq_zero_of_bondRule","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L184-L188","doc":"And the four-body cumulant with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.b3_eq_zero_of_bondRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.b3_eq_zero_of_bondRule","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**The conclusion.** The connected three-body cumulant of any trace-derived\nbinding vanishes identically. Not small — zero, for every `f`, every `μ`, and\nevery triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.bindingOfTrace_isPairwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.bindingOfTrace_isPairwise","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L157-L173","doc":"**The composition.** Under the bond rule and the Cauchy condition, a binding\nread off the trace is pairwise-additive — the property\n`PairwiseCumulantVanishing` shows kills every connected cumulant above two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.bindingOfTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.bindingOfTrace","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L150-L155","doc":"The binding read off the cluster traces by `f`, cluster by cluster. This is\nthe production shape: `B = -α · ln (tr_atom / tr_free)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.IsAdditiveOnProducts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.IsAdditiveOnProducts","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L145-L148","doc":"`f` carries products to sums — §10a's Cauchy condition, and **nothing more**:\nno continuity, no measurability, no regularity. The uniqueness step that would\npin `f` to a logarithm is not assumed and is not needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.SatisfiesBondRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.SatisfiesBondRule","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L135-L141","doc":"**The bond rule** (bean `qou-g8i1`): every cluster's trace ratio is the\nproduct of its bonds' factors. Carried as a hypothesis, not asserted — see the\nheader. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.quad","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L131-L131","doc":"the four-body cluster. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.triple","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L129-L129","doc":"the three-body cluster `{i, j, k}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.pair","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L127-L127","doc":"the two-body cluster `{i, j}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.ClusterTrace","kind":"structure","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MarkovBondRuleForcesPairwise.lean#L122-L131","doc":"The Markov-trace ratios of the clusters of up to four nucleons: one scalar per\ncluster. Only the *ratio* `tr_free / tr_atom` matters, so this carries no units\nand no anchor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}